+# 2026-10-21-external-turn-ownership
+
+English | [中文](2026-10-21-external-turn-ownership.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Adds required durable external turn ownership and explicit same-turn recovery.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Declaration](#declaration)
+- [Compatibility](#compatibility)
+- [Verification](#verification)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+<a id="declaration"></a>
+## Declaration
+
+```yaml persistence-change
+schemaVersion: 1
+id: 2026-10-21-external-turn-ownership
+baseline: false
+changes:
+  - root: "event:turn/owner"
+    previous: null
+    after: "6c18d530ae7cba12956444baaa0ba50a2ab08d9d69dd38725415eeee7bb19472"
+    decision: same-version
+```
+
+<a id="compatibility"></a>
+## Compatibility
+
+Existing logs without turn/owner retain ordinary interrupted-tail repair. The new discriminator is required-on-read and not ignorable, so older known-event readers reject it before recovery truncation. New readers preserve owned tails and require an explicit trusted engine with the original preset. Forks still synthesize their own closers. The header version is unchanged; unsupported data is refused rather than interpreted with old execution semantics.
+
+<a id="verification"></a>
+## Verification
+
+Node 26 and Node 22: focused external-turn recovery, execute-turn, resume and Session repair tests, 91 passed each; leaf agent-loop TypeScript build passed.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+## Dev Note
+
+None.
