+---
+kind: upgrade-guide
+description: Sessions claimed by an external whole-turn engine require a reader that understands durable turn ownership.
+---
+
+# External turn ownership
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+Opted-in whole-turn engines write required `turn/owner` events. Older readers reject these logs instead of repairing a delegated turn as a default-loop interruption. Ordinary logs are unchanged.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Keep a Host build supporting `dsh.external-turn-host/v1` when opening a claimed Session. Do not remove ownership events to make an older build accept it.
+2. Resolve the original engine and preset, inspect `agent.externalTurns.pending()`, then use `resume(engine, execute)`. The engine must verify its own stored admission and side effects.
+3. Confirm the original turn closes once and queued input runs only after recovery settles. A failed recovery keeps the turn open for explicit retry.
